Translation patch: <VartimeRistrettoPrecomputation as VartimePrecomputedMultiscalarMul>::new

Change: the lazy `static_points.map(|P| P.borrow().0)` becomes a `Vec` built by a helper.
Why: Aeneas only models `Iterator::next` (aeneas#1057). Loops over a generic `IntoIterator` don't extract, hence the nested `It: Iterator` helper.
Behaviour: identical (the callee consumes its input immediately).

diff --git a/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs b/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
index 269662d..85d6fb5 100644
--- a/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
+++ b/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
@@ -1010,10 +1010,14 @@ impl VartimePrecomputedMultiscalarMul for VartimeRistrettoPrecomputation {
     fn new<I>(static_points: I) -> Self
     where
         I: IntoIterator,
         I::Item: Borrow<Self::Point>,
     {
+        let mut extended_points = vec![];
+        for P in static_points {
+            extended_points.push(P.borrow().0);
+        }
         Self(crate::backend::VartimePrecomputedStraus::new(
-            static_points.into_iter().map(|P| P.borrow().0),
+            extended_points,
         ))
     }
 
